00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:27.382
Now more than half a century before Stephen Hawkings and Elon Musk

00:06:27.382 --> 00:06:30.060
felt compelled to warn the world of artificial intelligence

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:33.100
back in 1942, before the term was even coined,

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:41.660
the science fiction writer Isaac Asimov wrote the three laws of robotics a moral code to

00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:48.330
keep our machines in check. And the three
laws of robotics are: A robot may not injure

00:06:48.330 --> 00:06:53.480
a human being or through inaction allow a
human being to come to harm.

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:58.740
The second law, a robot must obey orders given by human beings except for such

00:06:58.840 --> 00:07:02.240
orders would conflict with the first law.

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:07.319
And the third, a robot must
protect its own existence as long as such

00:07:07.319 --> 00:07:11.160
protection does not conflict with the first
and the second law.

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:12.600
That sounds logical.

00:07:12.600 --> 00:07:14.200
Do these three laws provide a basis to work from to develop moral robots.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:20.480
Marcus what do you think?

00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:26.100
I think they make for good science fiction. There are lots of plots that you can turn around

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:28.500
having these kinds of laws.

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:33.479
But the first problem, if you've ever programed anything is
a concept like harm is really hard to program

00:07:33.479 --> 00:07:37.580
into a machine. It's one thing to program
in geometry or compound interest or something

00:07:37.580 --> 00:07:41.629
like that where we have precise necessary
and sufficient conditions. Nobody has any

00:07:41.629 --> 00:07:46.370
idea how to, in a generalized way get a machine
to recognize something like harm or justice.

00:07:46.370 --> 00:07:51.920
So there is a very serious programming problem.
Then there are a couple of other problems too.

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:54.319
One is that not everybody would agree
that the robot should never allow a human

00:07:54.319 --> 00:07:58.750
to come to harm and would it what if for example
we're talking about a terrorist or a sniper

00:07:58.750 --> 00:08:02.110
or something like that. I mean some people
not everybody but some people might actually

00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:05.810
want to allow that into what they would let
robots do.

00:08:05.810 --> 00:08:10.229
And then the third issue. You really think
through the third one of those laws is it

00:08:10.229 --> 00:08:14.629
sets up robots to be second class citizens
and ultimately to be slaves. And right now

00:08:14.629 --> 00:08:18.240
that might seem ok because robots don't seem
very clever but as they get smarter and smarter

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:21.580
they might resent that or it might not feel
like appropriate thing to do.

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:23.240
You mean those laws might not be fair to robots?

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:27.460
They might not be fair to robots. Exactly what I'm saying.

00:08:27.460 --> 00:08:29.810
